    {"id": 8, "type": "manual", "slot": "(c) written explanation",
     "desc": "Rubric for part (c): the response must say that a 9 percent annual drop is applied to a shrinking base each year, so the decreases compound (multiply) rather than add. A correct answer states that the model multiplies by 0.91 ten times, giving about a 61.1 percent total drop, and that adding 9 percent ten times would only be right if the same fixed amount were removed each year. Full credit needs the multiplicative reason, not just the number.",
